    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**## Initial Data Quality Visualization**\n",
        "\n",
        "*The initial exploratory plots revealed extreme numerical values\n",
        "in some environmental and logistics variables. These observations\n",
        "indicate that further data-quality investigation is required before\n",
        "using these variables for business analysis.*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "eLa99-0RQl-l"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Check the minimum and maximum values of important numerical columns.\n",
        "# This helps us identify unusually large or unusually small values.\n",
        "\n",
        "columns_to_check = [\n",
        "    \"Temperature\",\n",
        "    \"Route_Distance\",\n",
        "    \"Delivery_Time\",\n",
        "    \"Spoilage_Risk\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nMinimum and maximum values:\")\n",
        "\n",
        "for column in columns_to_check:\n",
        "    print(\n",
        "        column,\n",
        "        \"-> Min:\", df[column].min(),\n",
        "        \"| Max:\", df[column].max()\n",
        "    )"
      ],
      "metadata": {
